  "question": {
    ":question/id": "e7730023-e057-556f-9f2e-3b8b6248bde2",
    ":question/problem": "Find $AB,$ if $A=\\begin{bmatrix}1 \\\\ -1 \\\\ 0\\end{bmatrix}$\nand \n$B=\\begin{bmatrix}1 & -1\\end{bmatrix}.$",
    ":question/difficulty": ":question.difficulty/easy",
    ":question/worked-solution": "Here, $A$ is $3\\times 1$ matrix and $B$ is a $1\\times 2$ matrix.  \n\nThere is $1$ column in matrix $A$ and $1$ row in matrix $B$, so the product is well defined:\n\n$$\n{A}_{3\\times \\boxed{\\text{1}}}{\\cdot }_{✓}{B}_{\\boxed{\\text{1}}\\times 2}={AB}_{3\\times 2}\n$$\n\nComputing the product, we have\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}AB & =\\begin{bmatrix}1 \\\\ -1 \\\\ 0\\end{bmatrix}\\begin{bmatrix}1 & -1\\end{bmatrix} \\\\  & =\\begin{bmatrix}1\\cdot 1 & 1\\cdot (-1) \\\\ (-1)\\cdot 1 & (-1)\\cdot (-1) \\\\ 0\\cdot 1 & 0\\cdot (-1)\\end{bmatrix} \\\\  & =\\begin{bmatrix}1 & -1 \\\\ -1 & 1 \\\\ 0 & 0\\end{bmatrix}.\\end{aligned}\n$$",
